{"id": "EUVD-2026-81802", "enisaUuid": "0087544e-91cb-3cc4-9b14-868665a19df7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/debug: Fix deadlock during unregister\n\nUnregistering an s390dbf debug area while one of the associated debugfs\nfiles is being written to can cause a deadlock:\n\n$ echo >.../vmur/level    $ rmmod vmur\n===================================================\ndebugfs write\ndebugfs_file_get()\n                          debug_unregister()\n                          mutex_lock(debug_mutex)\n                          debugfs_remove()\n                          wait for debugfs_file_put()\ndebug_file_ops.write()\ndebug_input()\nmutex_lock(debug_mutex) ==> DEADLOCK\n\nFix this by splitting debug_unregister() into an s390dbf and debugfs\npart, and running only the s390dbf part with debug_mutex locked.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a214c3dacc779b2afcb0ac9c8001e45ee4ffb2ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/183f8f6d64bb0510070c856b9927618c53014a7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a08b70ed2d1ec907353a72f15163b8e34ff4b2f8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/45bb341d1b73eb293e0dd43d9b72bbc8b615d0ba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d83f3faa3fb7f23f298cfd40382611999de5d1d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/54e1259b75d6402a1d0cfb822b9bb2c507e53dab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/445c31ac638fd1af203d79bdf25fc0cb3149fbbc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5fhq-j2h9-6qrx", "CVE-2026-90209"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02ed396e-a6b9-34ba-b9d2-940e3f340799", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9372a82892c2caa6bccab9a4081166fa769699f8 <45bb341d1b73eb293e0dd43d9b72bbc8b615d0ba"}, {"id": "09cbb24d-86e5-3485-be83-9159ef1d004c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "19a004a1